Package: epiLabR
Type: Package
Title: Educational Framework for Compartmental Epidemiological Modelling
Version: 0.3.0
Author: Vicente Castellar [aut, cre]
Authors@R:
    person("Vicente", "Castellar",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "vic.sebastia@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for simulating deterministic compartmental epidemiological
    models defined by systems of ordinary differential equations (ODEs). The
    package allows users to define custom epidemic models, simulate state
    trajectories over time, and explore model behavior under different
    parameter settings. It includes implementations of classical compartmental
    models such as susceptible-infectious-recovered (SIR) models and related
    extensions. An optional 'shiny' application is provided for interactive
    visualization and exploration of epidemic scenarios. The methodological framework is based on:
    Anderson, R. M., & May, R. M. (1991). Infectious Diseases of Humans: Dynamics and Control. Oxford University 
    Press. <doi:10.1093/oso/9780198540403.001.0001>
    Hethcote, H. W. (2000). The Mathematics of Infectious Diseases. SIAM Review, 42(4), 599–653. <doi:10.1137/S0036144500371907>
    Keeling, M. J., & Rohani, P. (2008). Modeling Infectious Diseases in Humans and Animals. Princeton University Press. <doi:10.1515/9781400841035>
